      "text": [
        " الَّذِي يَخْضِبُ رَأْسَهُ بِالْحِنَّاءِ ثُمَّ يَبْدُو لَهُ فِي الْوُضُوءِ قَالَ لَا يَجُوزُ حَتَّى يُصِيبَ بَشَرَةَ رَأْسِهِ بِالْمَاءِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, ",
          "(It has been narrated) raising it from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the one who dyes his head with the henna, then it becomes inevitable for him with regards to the Ablution <span class=\"iTxt\">(Wudhu)</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He is not allowed until he pours in the hair of his head with the water’ (attached to his hands)."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. Muhammad ibn Yahya in a marfu‘ manner has narrated from the following: “About a man who dyes his head with henna and notices it during Wudu’, abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al- Salam, has said, ‘It is not permissible until water reaches the skin of his head.’” "
        ]
      }
